From f496120dbefcfdfd1c19109b06bc6354d9e92fb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:30:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add Samsung SOFEF03F M FHD DSC panel

Add a driver for the 1080x2400 command mode AMOLED panel used on the
OnePlus 7T.  The init sequence, PPS payload and DSC parameters are taken
verbatim from the vendor device tree node.

The backlight is driven through DCS 0x51 with the big-endian ("Samsung")
byte order, i.e. the vendor's qcom,mdss-bl-high2bit.  In normal mode the
register is 10 bits wide (0..1023).  The vendor driver encodes HBM as
"level + 1023", so writing 1024..2046 without switching the panel to the
high-brightness gamma first wraps around and makes the screen go dark;
clamp to 1023 and start at half scale.  Levels 1..5 flicker, so clamp
them up to 6 while leaving 0 alone for userspace.  The top of the range
switches to the vendor's high-brightness gamma with the sequence from
qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-hbm-brightness-on-command, and leaving it turns that
off again.

The panel runs at 90 Hz, the vendor's default timing, in a single fixed
mode.

An ESD check can run every two seconds: register 0x0a is read in LP mode
and must return 0x9c.  On mismatch the panel is power cycled,
re-initialised and its brightness restored.  It is opt-in via the
esd-check-enabled (or vendor qcom,esd-check-enabled) DT property and off
by default: the DCS read contends with the command-mode MDP stream and a
false positive power-cycles a panel with a live pipeline.

The first DSI command burst after power-on occasionally times out,
leaving the panel uninitialised behind a lit but black screen; retry the
init sequence with a power cycle up to three times.

Signed-off-by: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |  12 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile                |   1 +
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-sofef03f.c    | 667 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 680 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-sofef03f.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
index 5a582ecc2..ddf2be128 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
@@ -941,6 +941,18 @@ config DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_SOFEF00
 
 	    Samsung AMS628NW01 (found in OnePlus 6, 1080x2280@60Hz)
 
+config DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_SOFEF03F
+	tristate "Samsung SOFEF03F M FHD DSI panel (OnePlus 7T)"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	select VIDEOMODE_HELPERS
